WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.568
In the year 960, the Later Zhou general Zhao Kuangyin led his army northward.

00:00:08.918 --> 00:00:13.430
The soldiers were full of energy, marching forward in neat, even steps.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:19.732
When the army reached Chenqiao station, the soldiers suddenly grew noisy and restless — a mutiny had begun.

00:00:20.082 --> 00:00:25.866
Before the night had lifted, waves of shouting already rose from the camp.

00:00:26.216 --> 00:00:32.744
The soldiers draped a yellow robe over Zhao Kuangyin's shoulders and proclaimed him emperor.

00:00:33.094 --> 00:00:37.390
Zhao Kuangyin was both startled and delighted, and for a moment could not speak.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:43.908
Everyone knelt and shouted 'Long live the emperor!', and the cheers echoed through the whole camp.

00:00:44.258 --> 00:00:49.298
Zhao Kuangyin returned to Kaifeng and took over the capital without shedding a drop of blood.

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:55.216
Thus the Song dynasty was founded, and the chaos of the Five Dynasties in the Central Plain finally ended.

00:00:55.566 --> 00:01:00.822
From then on, the people welcomed a new unity and peace.

